  "id": "COMPOUND:25581 - PROTEIN:5944",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Calabaxanthone may interact with Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8 through a series of target relationships. The drug is linked to 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate and Lethedioside B. Both of these compounds are also targets of Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8, indicating a potential pathway where Calabaxanthone could influence the kinase activity of this enzyme. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The evidence highlights a possible role of the proteasome regulatory subunit in mediating the effects of Calabaxanthone, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction with the kinase.",
